<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, traditionally dated to 911, was an agreement between the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a>. Charles granted Rollo lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a> near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> in return for defending them against other raiders and accepting baptism. The grant was the origin of the Duchy of Normandy, although no text of the agreement survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-clair-sur-epte.jpg" alt="Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Alexandrin at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:France_%C3%A0_la_fin_du_Xe_si%C3%A8cle.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
